# __PACKAGE_NAME__

An [MDP](https://github.com/barmoshe/mdp) **block** extension.

> Scaffolded with `create-mdp-extension`. This starter renders a labeled row of
> tag pills; edit `src/index.mjs` to make it your own block.

## Try it

```sh
npm test          # markup, escaping, the design lock, determinism
npm run demo      # writes dist/preview.html - open it in a browser
```

Zero dependencies: it runs anywhere Node 18+ does.

## The source it's designed for

A block adds a fenced directive the host turns into an IR node:

````
```__FENCE__
label: Stack
tags: Node, ESM, Zero-dep
```
````

The IR node this package renders:

```js
{ type: "__NODE_TYPE__", label, tags: [string, ...] }
```

It exports the engine's block shape - a STYLE string and a render function:

```js
import { __RENDER_FN__, __STYLE_CONST__ } from "__PACKAGE_NAME__";
```

## Publish (the convention)

MDP discovers extensions with no central registry - just npm + GitHub search:

1. Keep `"keywords": ["mdp", "__KEYWORD__"]` in `package.json` (already set).
2. `npm publish`
3. Add the **`__KEYWORD__`** topic to the GitHub repo.

It's then found by `npm search keywords:__KEYWORD__` and GitHub's `__KEYWORD__`
topic page.

## Use it in a document

`@mdp/core` has no runtime plugin loader yet, so the host wires a block in. To
render `__FENCE__` in a real page / slides / flyer, fork or patch
[`@mdp/core`](https://github.com/barmoshe/mdp) and:

1. **Parse** - in `packages/core/src/parse.mjs`, emit the node for your fence
   (model it on the `mdp:compare` branch):

   ```js
   } else if (fenceInfo === "__FENCE__") {
     blocks.push({ type: "__NODE_TYPE__", /* ...parse bodyLines... */ });
   }
   ```

2. **Render** - in each of `render-page.mjs`, `render-slides.mjs`,
   `render-flyer.mjs`, import this package, add a case to the block switch, and
   inject the STYLE where the other block styles are injected:

   ```js
   import { __RENDER_FN__, __STYLE_CONST__ } from "__PACKAGE_NAME__";
   // in the stylesheet:  ${__STYLE_CONST__}
   // in renderBlock:     case "__NODE_TYPE__": return __RENDER_FN__(block);
   ```

3. **Wire the interactive forms** - in `packages/core/src/content-blocks.mjs`, add
   the same case to `renderContentBlock` and add your STYLE to the
   `CONTENT_BLOCK_STYLE` array. That one file is what renders the block in the four
   interactive forms (scroll, accordion, tabs, stepper); a block wired only into
   page/slides/flyer shows up blank in them.

   ```js
   import { __RENDER_FN__, __STYLE_CONST__ } from "__PACKAGE_NAME__";
   // add __STYLE_CONST__ to the CONTENT_BLOCK_STYLE array
   // in renderContentBlock:  case "__NODE_TYPE__": return __RENDER_FN__(block);
   ```

An unknown fence already degrades to readable text, so an un-wired block never
breaks a document.

